          "lead_raw_text": " The structure of LiHg₃ (Z = 8 per cell) crystallizes in the hexagonal space group P6₃/mmc (No. 194), with two independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows both Hg and Li centers adopt close-packed-like 12-neighbor arrangements; Hg is surrounded by 8 Hg and 4 Li, while Li is surrounded by 12 Hg, with neighbor distances ranging from about 3.21 to 3.26 Å. The periodic neighbor graph forms a single 3D-connected component containing all 8 sites. Validated polyhedron contacts reveal Hg–Hg 12-vertex polyhedra sharing corners, edges, and faces, and Hg–Li polyhedra sharing corners and edges.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
